---
import config from '../data/contact.json';
---
{config.enabled && <section id="contact-messages"><h2>Messages sent through our contact form</h2><p>We use Formspree to receive contact messages. If you submit the form, your email address, optional name, selected topic, message, and technical request information are processed by Formspree and our email providers so we can receive and answer your enquiry. The submission service may require a Google reCAPTCHA spam check. The form does not subscribe you to a mailing list.</p><p>Contact-message processing is separate from optional Google Analytics. Our own analytics code does not send the contents of contact fields. We do not embed Formspree or reCAPTCHA scripts in this page; submission and any spam check take place through the submission service. See <a href="https://formspree.io/legal/privacy-policy/" rel="noopener noreferrer">Formspree's privacy policy</a> and <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google's privacy policy</a>.</p><p>Messages may be processed outside your country. Please do not include passwords, payment details, or sensitive personal information. You may use the <a href="/contact/">contact form</a> for a question about a message you previously sent. We use messages to handle enquiries and maintain relevant correspondence; a specific retention period for correspondence has not yet been established.</p></section>}
